es up about 120 days of sales, a drag on cash generation."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 11.1% over 3 years, 4.8% over 5 years and 5.3% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 19%).","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 18.7% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -15.4% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.17 (orders outpacing sales), a backlog worth 40% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 39%.","Capex runs only 0.8x depreciation (2.0% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 7, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.2%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (11 sales, net $21.8M sold).","Net share issuance leaves shareholder yield negative (-7.2%), diluting holders."],"people":["With about 4,100 employees, each generates about $370K of revenue, in line with the Technology median.","That works out to $20K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.2M (6x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $14K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":44,"head":"Avoid: priced 133% above its fair value of $13.19.","pros":["ROIC 18.7% vs WACC 10.1%","Net debt/EBITDA -4.5x","7 analysts' mean target $56.00 (+82%)","12-1 month momentum +144%"],"cons":["Trades 133% above fair value of $13.19","Interest coverage only 2.2x","Altman Z in the distress zone (-31.51)","P/E 118.2x vs sector 27.4x","EV/EBITDA 22.0x vs sector 17.1x"],"flags":["Priced 133% above its fair value of $13.19"],"need":[],"buy_below":11.21,"vc":{"base":13.19,"base_src":"dcf","bear":8.83,"bull":20.89,"alt_median":2.25,"n_alt":2,"gap":4.8596,"d